  "attack_progression": [
    {"step": 1, "tactic": "Initial Access (Valid Account)", "technique": "T1078.002", "what_happened": "At 2026-09-11 19:00:42 CEST, Event 4624 'An account was successfully logged on' fired on FILESVR-CORP-01 (10.30.5.18): TargetUserName=amir.z, logonType=3 (Network — SMB share access), IpAddress=10.30.7.91 (his own workstation WS-FIN-23). The auth itself is legitimate — amir.z is still an active employee — but his HR record is flagged RESIGNED with last day in 7 days (resignation submitted 1 week ago). The legitimate-but-departing-employee context turns ordinary SMB access into elevated risk.", "chain_reason": "Windows Security Event 4624 logonType=3 on FILESVR-CORP-01 from amir.z@10.30.7.91. Correlation key: HR-feed flag 'amir.z = RESIGNED, last_day_offset_days=7' fused with auth event at SIEM enrichment time.", "first_seen": "2026-09-11T19:00:42+0200"},
    {"step": 2, "tactic": "Collection (Data Staged — Local)", "technique": "T1074.001 + T1039", "what_happened": "Between 19:02:14 and 19:02:42 (28 seconds), Event 4663 'An attempt was made to access an object' fired 87 times on FILESVR-CORP-01 with SubjectUserName=amir.z, AccessList=%%4416 (ReadData), spanning ObjectName paths across \\\\FILESVR-CORP-01\\finance\\* and \\\\FILESVR-CORP-01\\legal\\*. Sample ObjectName values: \\\\FILESVR-CORP-01\\finance\\payroll\\2025_salaries.xlsx (19:02:14), \\\\FILESVR-CORP-01\\finance\\customer_master.csv (19:02:16), \\\\FILESVR-CORP-01\\legal\\contracts\\all_active.pdf (19:02:19). The Wazuh decoder fires VOLUME ANOMALY: amir.z read 87 files in 28s = ~3.1 files/sec, against baseline ~5 files/HOUR for this user on these shares. The ~600× rate spike combined with cross-share span (finance + legal — two unrelated business domains amir.z has no day-to-day reason to BOTH access at once) is the diagnostic of mass-collection, not legitimate work.", "chain_reason": "Windows Security Event 4663 burst correlation rule (rule.id 60412, level 12). Signature: same SubjectUserName + ReadData AccessList + count >= 50 in <= 60 s + spanning >= 2 top-level share roots.", "first_seen": "2026-09-11T19:02:14+0200"},
    {"step": 3, "tactic": "Collection (Data Staged — Local Archive)", "technique": "T1074.001 + T1560.001", "what_happened": "At 19:05:11, Sysmon Event 11 'FileCreate' fired on WS-FIN-23 (10.30.7.91) with TargetFilename=C:\\Users\\amir.z\\Documents\\backup.zip. At 19:05:21 (10 seconds later), Sysmon Event 1 'Process Create' fired with Image=7z.exe, CommandLine='7z.exe a -tzip C:\\Users\\amir.z\\Documents\\backup.zip C:\\Users\\amir.z\\Documents\\staging\\* -p\"strong-pwd-123\"', ParentImage=explorer.exe, User=CORP\\amir.z. CRITICAL FLAG: the archive is PASSWORD-PROTECTED (-p\"strong-pwd-123\"). Password-protected archives ENCRYPT both the file content AND the central directory — DLP / mail gateway / proxy content inspection CANNOT read what's inside. The choice to password-protect a 'backup' of one's own work documents is a deliberate DLP-evasion technique, not standard backup behavior. Final size at 19:06:02 (Sysmon Event 11 close-write): 1.2 GB.", "chain_reason": "Sysmon Event 11 (TargetFilename=C:\\Users\\amir.z\\Documents\\backup.zip) followed within 10s by Sysmon Event 1 with image=7z.exe and commandLine containing '-p' (password flag). The temporal coupling + the -p flag combined with the upstream Event 4663 mass-read burst on FILESVR-CORP-01 is the staged-exfil archive signature.", "first_seen": "2026-09-11T19:05:11+0200"},
    {"step": 4, "tactic": "Exfiltration (Over Physical Medium — USB)", "technique": "T1052.001", "what_happened": "At 19:08:18, Sysmon Event 1 fired on WS-FIN-23 with Image=cmd.exe, CommandLine='cmd.exe /c xcopy C:\\Users\\amir.z\\Documents\\backup.zip E:\\', ParentImage=explorer.exe, User=CORP\\amir.z. The E:\\ drive is NOT a fixed disk on WS-FIN-23 (CMDB confirms WS-FIN-23 has only C:\\ + D:\\ fixed disks). At 19:09:18 (60 seconds later — consistent with the USB enumeration + first-write window), Windows Security Event 6416 'An external device was recognized by the system' fired on WS-FIN-23 with DeviceClass=USBSTOR, DeviceName='SanDisk Ultra USB 3.0'. The combined sequence — xcopy of the password-protected archive to E:\\ followed by USBSTOR recognition of a removable drive — is the textbook physical-medium exfil signature (T1052.001).", "chain_reason": "Sysmon Event 1 (image=cmd.exe + commandLine contains 'xcopy' + 'E:\\\\') temporally adjacent (60s window) to Windows Security Event 6416 (DeviceClass=USBSTOR) on the same agent.name. The xcopy destination drive letter aligns with the dynamically-mounted USB drive.", "first_seen": "2026-09-11T19:08:18+0200"}
  ],
